        "answer": {
          "short": "\\$17 554.77 income tax",
          "worked": "The taxable income is in the \\$80 001–\\$180 000 bracket.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Excess} &= 80\\,021-80\\,000\\\\\\text{Excess} &= \\$21\\\\\\text{Income tax} &= 17\\,547+0.37\\times21\\\\\\text{Income tax} &= \\$17\\,554.77\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p72-q16-refund",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "In addition to the above tax, Theo must also pay a Medicare levy of \\$1600.42.\nTheo has already paid \\$20 525 as Pay as You Go (PAYG) tax.\nShould Theo receive a tax refund, or will he owe more tax? Justify your answer.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Refund of \\$1369.81; PAYG paid exceeds total tax payable.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Total tax payable} &= 17\\,554.77+1600.42\\\\\\text{Total tax payable} &= \\$19\\,155.19\\\\\\text{Instalments}-\\text{Total tax payable} &= 20\\,525-19\\,155.19\\\\\\text{Instalments}-\\text{Total tax payable} &= \\$1369.81\\end{align*}$$\nTheo receives a refund of \\$1369.81 because his PAYG payments exceed his total tax payable.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
